.prose
  :markdown
    # Memoization

    Memoization is the simplest performance tool there is: compute a value
    once, hand back the same answer every time after. Ruby's idiom for it —
    `@value ||= compute` — is so short that it hides three real bugs, and
    fixing them by hand produces exactly the kind of boilerplate a library
    should own. This guide covers why we use
    [memo_wise](https://github.com/panorama-ed/memo_wise), how to use it,
    and — the part that matters more than the syntax — when memoizing is the
    wrong call.

